⚠️ severity: IMPORTANT —
⚠️ **IMPORTANT: the busy-phase `try/finally` guard was dropped from both relief call sites**

The old code cleared the `Compacting context…` busy label in a `finally`:

```dart
_pushBusyPhase('Compacting context…');
try {
  await _runAutoCompact('[auto-compacted]');
} finally {
  _pushBusyPhase('');
}
```

The new code clears it only on the success path:

```dart
_pushBusyPhase('Compacting context…');
final reliefOutcome = await _runEmergencyRelief();
_pushBusyPhase('');
```

`EmergencyRelief.run()`'s own failure-safety covers only `appendHiddenRange`
(`emergency_relief.dart:319-329`). Its re-anchor and view-build I/O —
`refreshAgentState` → `session.buildContextMessages()` (line 186), and
`session.getBranch()`/`session.getEntries()` in `_buildView` (lines 336-341) —
sit OUTSIDE that guard and can still throw (torn/corrupt session JSONL, I/O
failure). On such a throw the label is never cleared: the loop's `catch (_)`
(agent_loop.dart:1624) turns the relief into "no relief" and the turn ends on
the terminal guard error — printed under a stuck `Compacting context…` busy
row. That is exactly the "reads as a dead stall" face the removed `finally`
was introduced to prevent (issue #1085 M3, comment right above this line).

The window is bounded (the row drops when the run settles), but the regression
is on the exact lines this PR rewrote and costs one line to restore. Please
wrap the relief await in `try/finally` in BOTH sites (`_relieveOverWindow` and
`_relieveMessageCap`, same shape at line 1002-1004).
